['1. Utilize `HttpClient` with `Task` to fetch weather data asynchronously. Implement caching using in-memory store (e.g., ConcurrentDictionary) and Redis for distributed caching.

```csharp
var httpClient = new HttpClient();
var redisCache = new RedisCache();

public async Task<WeatherData> GetWeatherDataAsync(string location)
{
    if (redisCache.ContainsKey(location))
        return redisCache[location];

    var weatherData = await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<WeatherData>($"http://weather-api/{location}").ConfigureAwait(false);
    redisCache.Set(location, weatherData);
    return weatherData;
}
```

2. Implement resilient architecture using Polly for circuit breaker pattern and retry policies, HandleInvalidJsonException to handle invalid JSON responses, and implement custom logging and alerting mechanisms using Serilog and SignalR notifications.

