   Assuming you have a parent window (parentWindow) and a dialog component with field names stored in an array, updateFields():

```javascript
function updateFields(fieldNames) {
  if (!Array.isArray(fieldNames)) {
    throw new Error('fieldNames must be an array.');
  }

  parentWindow.postMessage({ command: 'updateFields', data: fieldNames }, '*');

  // Listen for response from the parent window and update fields if successful
  window.addEventListener('message', (event) => {
    if (event.data && event.data.command === 'updateFieldsResponse') {
      const { fields, success } = event.data.data;
      if (success && Array.isArray(fields)) {
        fieldNames.forEach((fieldName, index) => {
          document.querySelector(`#${fieldName}`).value = fields[index];
        });
      }
    }
  }, false);
}
```

This function sends a message to the parent window with the field names to be updated, and listens for a response indicating whether the update was successful. If successful, it updates the dialog fields based on the provided array of field names. The function handles errors by throwing an error if the fieldNames parameter is not an array.

