Configure EhCache cache manager, eviction policy, and other properties within a configuration class:

```java
@Configuration
@EnableCaching
public class CacheConfig extends CacheManagerFactoryBean {

  @Value("${cache.maxSize}")
  private int maxSize;

  @Value("${cache.evictionPolicy}")
  private String evictionPolicy;

  // Additional properties and constructors

  @Override
  public EhCacheCacheManager createCacheManager() {
    CacheManager cacheManager = new EhCacheManager();

    Configuration config = new Configuration();
    config.addResourceLoader(new ClassPathResourceLoader());

    if (evictionPolicy != null) {
      config.setEvictionPolicy(evictionPolicy);
    } else {
      config.setEvictionPolicy(EvictionPolicy.LFU);
    }

    config.setMaxElementsInMemory(maxSize);

    cacheManager.setConfiguration(config);

    return (EhCacheCacheManager) cacheManager;
  }
}
```

