["```cpp
#include <forward_list>
#include <algorithm>
#include <iterator>
#include <stdexcept>

void insertAfter(std::forward_list<std::string>& list, const std::string& target, const std::string& value) {
    if (list.empty()) {
        list.push_back(target);
        list.push_back(value);
        return;
    }

    auto it = list.begin();
    auto end = list.end();

    while (it != end) {
        if (*it == target) {
            list.insert after_iterator(it, value);
            return;
        }
        ++it;
    }

    list.push_back(target);
    list.push_back(value);
}
```
This function modifies the given forward list by inserting the second argument after the first one if found, or appending it to the end of the list otherwise. The function uses C++11's `std::forward_list`, `std::iterator`, and `std::after_iterator` to accomplish this task efficiently and in place. This function can be used in your caching solution to manage theme data dynamically based on user interactions and preferences."]

